Why GPL-3.0-or-later
--------------------

SleepRadio's "Broadcast Radio" mode uses on-device text-to-speech via
sherpa-onnx (https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx). sherpa-onnx itself is
Apache-2.0, but for Piper / VITS voices it statically links eSpeak-NG
(https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng) for phoneme generation, and eSpeak-NG
is licensed GPL-3.0-or-later. Because a released APK therefore contains
GPL-licensed code, the project as a whole is distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later.

Corresponding source is this repository:
https://github.com/dylan7474/SleepRadio


